# Locate a named object with the wrist/overhead camera and grasp it.
#
# Perception path: resolve robonix/primitive/camera/rgb via atlas -> grab one
# undistorted frame -> VLM open-vocabulary detection returns a pixel bbox ->
# 2D hand-eye homography maps the bbox centre to arm base_link XY -> the grasp
# is executed at [x, y, desktop_height] with the configured vertical-down RPY,
# reusing the same grasp segment as `grab`.
#
# Request carries the target: the LLM passes what the user asked for
# ("the red block" / "螺丝刀"), forwarded verbatim to the VLM locator.
string object
---
# Whether the pick completed (descended, closed, lifted back to hover).
bool success

# Human-readable status. On failure, names the failing stage
# (preflight / detect / geometry / approach / descend / pick/close / lift).
string message

# How long the whole call took (s).
float32 elapsed_s
